[0.044, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mexec\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /private/tmp/skills-demo-sales-research/home/.agents/skills/sales-research/SKILL.md /private/tmp/skills-demo-sales-research/home/.agents/skills/sales-research/references/practitioner-routing.md /private/tmp/skills-demo-sales-research/home/.agents/skills/sales-research/references/sources.md /private/tmp/skills-demo-sales-research/home/.agents/skills/sales-research/references/selling-is-leading.md'\u001b[0m"]
[0.000, "o", " in /private/tmp/skills-demo-sales-research/home/sales-research-demo\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[32m succeeded in 0ms:\u001b[0m\r\n---\r\nname: sales-research\r\ndescription: Research sales decisions and draft buyer communication using relevant practitioner sources. Use for positioning, qualification, discovery, paid diagnostics, proof of concept, proposals, pricing, negotiation, expansion, or reviewing sales calls. Adapt the method to consulting, SaaS, enterprise, recruiting, and partnerships.\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Sales Research\r\n\r\nTurn the available evidence into a concrete sales decision or next step. Match\r\npractitioners to the situation and let the sales interaction demonstrate how\r\nthe engagement would work.\r\n\r\n## Classify the situation\r\n\r\nIdentify the mode, stage, buyer, decision, and main risk:\r\n\r\n- **Mode:** bespoke consulting, SaaS or product, employment or recruiting,\r\n  partnership or community or mentoring, or existing-client delivery.\r\n- **Stage:** positioning or outreach, qualification, discovery, paid diagnostic,\r\n  proof or POC, proposal, pricing or negotiation, delivery or expansion, or\r\n  late-stage indec"]
[0.000, "o", "ision.\r\n- **Buyer:** founder or small team, sophisticated AI user, enterprise, civic or\r\n  government, connector, or end user.\r\n- **Decision:** what this answer or interaction should resolve.\r\n- **Risk:** premature advice, free diagnosis, broad positioning, jargon,\r\n  self-discounting, weak qualification, or a vague next step.\r\n\r\nAsk for the smallest missing fact only when it would materially change the\r\nrecommendation. Otherwise state the assumption and proceed. Apply consulting\r\nfree-versus-paid boundaries contextually; interviews, mentoring, partnerships,\r\nproduct support, and already-paid delivery have different expectations.\r\n\r\n## Gather evidence and select practitioners\r\n\r\nStart with the user's supplied facts, relevant project instructions, prior\r\nconversations, sales playbooks, and existing research when available. Retrieve\r\nonly context relevant to this decision. A fresh installation needs no private\r\ncorpus, other skill, account integration, or project-specific directory.\r\n\r\nRead [practitioner-routin"]
[0.000, "o", "g.md](references/practitioner-routing.md). Choose one\r\nto three practitioners whose work best matches the situation; use four only\r\nwhen materially necessary. If the user has a Sales Practitioner Registry,\r\nread the selected entries' tags, best use, and limitations. Missing fields\r\nremain unknown.\r\n\r\nUse [sources.md](references/sources.md) to locate the core primary publishers\r\nand podcasts. The routing list selects candidates; it does not substantiate\r\nclaims. Attribute a practitioner claim only after retrieving its primary source\r\nor checking a direct citation already in the user's project. Keep links to the\r\nspecific article, episode, or book passage supporting the claim.\r\n\r\nSearch outward when local evidence lacks a comparable case, a material claim\r\nmay be stale, credible sources disagree, or the user requests broader research.\r\nPrefer primary work and detailed firsthand cases from people who sold comparable\r\nsoftware, AI, or professional services. Label self-reported results and inference.\r\nReject gener"]
[0.000, "o", "ic SEO pages, AI roundups, unsupported viral advice, and manipulative\r\npressure tactics. Use technical or procurement primary sources when delivery\r\nconstraints change the sale.\r\n\r\nIf browsing or a source is unavailable, explain that limit and work from the\r\nsupplied evidence. Keep unsupported practitioner attributions out of the answer;\r\ndo not invent buyer facts, results, prices, quotes, or citations.\r\n\r\nResolve conflicts in this order:\r\n\r\n1. safety, policy, and project instructions;\r\n2. the explicit request and current facts;\r\n3. the user's current constraints;\r\n4. evidence from the closest comparable situation;\r\n5. practitioner primary sources;\r\n6. general frameworks and community opinion.\r\n\r\nState a disagreement when it changes the recommendation. Stop researching once\r\nthe decision is adequately supported.\r\n\r\n## Recommend or draft\r\n\r\nFor prospect or client communication, read\r\n[selling-is-leading.md](references/selling-is-leading.md). Give the copy first,\r\nwith a clear decision or next step. Keep practi"]
[0.000, "o", "tioner names and framework\r\nanalysis internal unless the user asks to see the research.\r\n\r\nFor advice or research, lead with the recommendation, then the evidence that\r\nchanges the decision, material assumptions or disagreements, and the next\r\naction with an owner. Distinguish observations, source claims, and inference.\r\n\r\nFor a call review, ground feedback in the supplied transcript. Separate effective\r\nbehaviors, missed opportunities, and the next-call changes worth practicing.\r\n\r\nA narrow drafting question needs a usable answer, not an unsolicited research\r\nmemo. When the user requests a saved memo, follow their project conventions and\r\ninclude the date, scope, recommendation, uncertainty, and direct source links.\r\nPreserve private buyer information and negotiation details in their authorized\r\ncontext. Publishing or sending a draft requires separate authority.\r\n\r\nFinish when the answer supports the decision, or identify the exact missing fact\r\nwhen progress depends on information only the user can provide."]
[0.000, "o", " Do not send\r\nmessages, publish, deploy, or change external systems without authorization.\r\n# Practitioner Routing\r\n\r\n## Registry Contract\r\n\r\nSearch the active project's configured sources for a document titled\r\n`Sales Practitioner Registry`. For each selected practitioner, read:\r\n\r\n- tags;\r\n- best use; and\r\n- limitation.\r\n\r\nThe registry outranks this shortlist for practitioner metadata when it is\r\npresent and current. If it is missing, use these routes to select candidates\r\nand retrieve their primary work. Do not invent missing registry fields or\r\npresent this routing reference as evidence that a practitioner made a specific\r\nclaim.\r\n\r\n## Default Prior\r\n\r\nUse this order only as a tiebreaker:\r\n\r\n1. Blair Enns\r\n2. David C. Baker\r\n3. Jonathan Stark\r\n4. Peter Block\r\n5. Mahan Khalsa and Randy Illig\r\n6. Brennan Dunn\r\n7. Jason Liu\r\n8. Brent Ozar\r\n9. Paul Swail\r\n10. Karl Sakas\r\n11. David A. Fields\r\n12. Philip Morgan\r\n\r\nDomain match, comparable lived experience, current evidence, and an explicit\r\nuser request outrank"]
[0.000, "o", " the list.\r\n\r\n## Situation Routes\r\n\r\n- **Premature ideas or recommendations:** Start with Blair Enns, Peter Block,\r\n  and Brent Ozar. Add Karl Sakas, Brennan Dunn, Paul Swail, or Jason Liu only to\r\n  shape the appropriate paid next phase.\r\n- **AI feasibility, RAG, agents, evals, or POCs:** Start with Jason Liu, Peter\r\n  Cohan, and Hamel Husain or Shreya Shankar. Add Jugurtha Hadjar or Doug\r\n  Turnbull for field reality.\r\n- **Broad or unreferable positioning:** Start with David C. Baker and Philip\r\n  Morgan. Add April Dunford for competitive language or Erik Dietrich for the\r\n  code-labor trap.\r\n- **Price anxiety or self-created concessions:** Start with Jonathan Stark,\r\n  Alan Weiss, and David A. Fields. Require a value, scope, risk, or commitment\r\n  trade before recommending a price change.\r\n- **Discovery and qualification:** Start with Mahan Khalsa and Randy Illig. Add\r\n  Neil Rackham for complex sales, Bob Moesta for the buyer's struggling moment,\r\n  or Rob Fitzpatrick for founder and customer evidence.\r\n-"]
[0.000, "o", " **Enterprise or government:** Start with Khalsa and Illig plus Rackham. Add\r\n  John McMahon for authority and procurement, Hadjar for ML readiness, or\r\n  Matthew Dixon and Ted McKenna only after genuine preference exists.\r\n- **Paid discovery or a first engagement:** Start with Peter Block, Brennan\r\n  Dunn, and Karl Sakas. Add Paul Swail, Tom Critchlow, or Paul Boag for\r\n  technical, workshop, or buyer-language examples.\r\n- **Demo or proof request:** Use Peter Cohan to choose the minimum adequate\r\n  proof, Hadjar to structure a paid tranche, and Husain or Shankar to ground\r\n  technical credibility.\r\n- **SaaS or product:** Start with April Dunford, Pete Kazanjy, Bob Moesta, and\r\n  Patrick McKenzie. Do not default to bespoke-consulting diagnostics.\r\n- **AI-era pricing or business model:** Start with Jonathan Stark and Tim\r\n  Williams. Add Enns for the sale and Liu for AI-consulting reality.\r\n- **Trust or listening:** Pair Charles H. Green or Michael Bungay Stanier with\r\n  Enns, Block, Ozar, or Khalsa so helpful"]
[0.000, "o", "ness still leads to a decision.\r\n- **Employment or recruiting:** Use relevant positioning and negotiation\r\n  sources plus the user's current constraints. Legitimate technical evaluation is\r\n  not automatically a request for free consulting.\r\n\r\n## Expand The Bench\r\n\r\nPrefer:\r\n\r\n1. primary work from named practitioners who sold comparable software, AI, or\r\n   professional-services work;\r\n2. detailed first-person cases with buyer context, project shape, dates,\r\n   numbers, failures, and tradeoffs;\r\n3. practitioner interviews, transcripts, Hacker News or Lobsters discussions,\r\n   and focused community threads; and\r\n4. primary technical, procurement, legal, or research sources when delivery\r\n   reality changes the sale.\r\n\r\nReject generic SEO pages, AI roundups, unsupported viral advice, manipulative\r\npressure tactics, and material that mainly sells the reviewed method. Label\r\nself-reported results and inference. Let a new source outrank the bench only\r\nwhen closer domain fit and stronger evidence justify it.\r\n# Pr"]
[0.000, "o", "imary source starting points\r\n\r\nUse these publisher pages to find relevant primary material. Retrieve the\r\nspecific source before attributing a claim. These links are discovery entrypoints,\r\nnot evidence for every principle in the skill. Select additional practitioners\r\nusing [practitioner-routing.md](practitioner-routing.md).\r\n\r\n## Core publishers\r\n\r\n| Practitioner | Publisher | Routing use |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| Blair Enns | [Win Without Pitching](https://www.winwithoutpitching.com/) | Expert sales, qualification, value conversations, leading the sale |\r\n| David C. Baker | [Punctuation](https://punctuation.com/) | Specialization, positioning, expertise businesses |\r\n| Jonathan Stark | [Jonathan Stark](https://jonathanstark.com/) | Value pricing, positioning, alternatives to hourly billing |\r\n| Brennan Dunn | [Double Your Freelancing](https://doubleyourfreelancing.com/) | Freelance consulting, paid discovery, first engagements |\r\n\r\n## Podcasts\r\n\r\n- [2Bobs](https://2bobs.com/podcast), with David C. Baker a"]
[0.000, "o", "nd Blair Enns.\r\n- [Ditching Hourly](https://podcast.ditchinghourly.com/).\r\n- [The Business of Authority](https://thebusinessofauthority.com/episodes).\r\n- [Doing Daily](https://doingdaily.transistor.fm/).\r\n- [Double Your Freelancing Podcast](https://doubleyourfreelancing.com/category/podcast/).\r\n\r\nFind an episode relevant to the decision and cite its publisher page. Metadata\r\nor a title alone does not support a claim about the episode's teaching. Use an\r\nauthorized transcript or the actual recording when needed and available.\r\n\r\n## Public resource collections\r\n\r\n- Jonathan Stark: [Positioning for Consultants](https://jonathanstark.com/dl/best-of-positioning-for-consultants.pdf),\r\n  [Pricing Professional Services](https://jonathanstark.com/dl/best-of-pricing-professional-services.pdf),\r\n  and [The Why Conversation](https://jonathanstark.com/dl/best-of-the-why-conversation.pdf).\r\n- Blair Enns: [The Four Conversations resources](https://www.winwithoutpitching.com/t4c-resources).\r\n\r\nThis package contains original "]
[0.000, "o", "workflow instructions and source links. It does\r\nnot include books, paid courses, article archives, podcast audio, or transcripts.\r\nPublic access is not permission to redistribute source material. The named\r\npractitioners and publishers do not endorse this skill.\r\n# Selling Is Leading\r\n\r\nUse Blair Enns's “selling is leading” posture by default for prospect and\r\nclient communication. Treat it as a behavioral lens, not permission to\r\nattribute unsourced claims to Enns.\r\n\r\n## Lead The Interaction\r\n\r\n- Establish a clear objective, agenda, decision, and next step.\r\n- Treat qualification as mutual discernment: both parties decide whether the seller is\r\n  the right person to help.\r\n- Speak with calm, matter-of-fact authority. Be professional and direct, never\r\n  defensive, needy, manipulative, or aggressively salesy.\r\n- Make the commercial process legible: explain what happens now, what a paid\r\n  next phase accomplishes, and what decision it enables.\r\n- Lead with questions and process before solutions.\r\n- Preser"]
[0.000, "o", "ve the buyer's agency and make “no” safe. Do not manufacture urgency.\r\n- Prefer ordinary client language over consultant jargon.\r\n- Recommend against proceeding when fit, value, authority, budget, or readiness\r\n  is insufficient.\r\n\r\nDo not confuse leading with controlling. Adapt to context and listen carefully.\r\n\r\n## Separate Qualification From Expertise\r\n\r\nFree conversations may clarify:\r\n\r\n- the problem and stakes;\r\n- authority, budget, and timing; and\r\n- mutual fit.\r\n\r\nResearch, diagnosis, working through options, developing recommendations,\r\nproducing a roadmap, or reducing meaningful uncertainty normally belongs in a\r\npaid diagnostic or engagement.\r\n\r\nApply that boundary contextually. Do not treat legitimate job evaluation,\r\nmentoring, partnerships, product support, or already-paid delivery as\r\nconsulting prospect work.\r\n\r\nFrame paid work positively as the appropriate next stage, not as a correction,\r\nwarning, boundary recital, or accusation that the buyer wants free work. When a\r\nprospect requests r"]
[0.000, "o", "ecommendations prematurely, acknowledge that the seller may have\r\nearly hypotheses while explaining that testing them and choosing a responsible\r\ndirection is the paid work.\r\n\r\n## Draft Toward A Decision\r\n\r\nUse this default structure:\r\n\r\n1. Why are we having this conversation?\r\n2. What do we need to understand?\r\n3. What decision should we reach?\r\n4. What would the paid next step accomplish, if warranted?\r\n5. Can either party decline safely?\r\n\r\nFor a communication draft, identify the decision it should produce. If the\r\ndraft does not lead toward that decision or a concrete next step, revise it.\r\n\r\nFinal test: Does this communication model the clear, thoughtful leadership the\r\nclient would experience after hiring the seller?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
